        "original_id": "2d88dda2-af5d-54d3-b289-6efef9e806a1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Robert A. Millikan, Harvey Fletcher, Robert Andrews Millikan\n- Experiments: oil drop experiment\n- Concepts: elementary electric charge, charge of the electron, photoelectric effect\n- Awards: Nobel Prize in Physics\n\nFacts:\n- In 1909, Robert A. Millikan and Harvey Fletcher performed the oil drop experiment to measure the elementary electric charge, which is the charge of the electron.\n- Robert Andrews Millikan was born on March 22, 1868, and died on December 19, 1953.\n- Robert Andrews Millikan was an American experimental physicist.\n- In 1923, Robert Andrews Millikan received the Nobel Prize in Physics for measuring the elementary electronic charge and for his work on the photoelectric effect.",
